eived fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm right breast mastectomy specimen with a stitch placed by the surgeon marking the axillary tail  The anterior portion is inked blue  and the posterior black  The specimen is thinly sectioned  No biopsy cavity or masses are noted  In the central inferior part of the breast there is white fibrous appearing tissue which is REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm in area  The remaining breast tissue is unremarkable  The axillary region is examined for lymph nodes  however no lymph nodes are present  The fibrous areas in the described region are sampled and the following cassettes are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area for reference to the remaining specimen  this area is marked with a single pin and is lateral to the other regions sampled   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area which for future reference is marked with two pins and is further medial to that sampled in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous area  which is marked with three pins for future reference and is more medial to that sampled in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of posterior margin  Following histologic examination of cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the specimen is taken to radiology and a surgical clip is identified near a region where sections were taken in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The region on the radiograph which displays the clip  located anterior inferiorly in the specimen  is blocked out and submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   A biopsy cavity with brownish tan tissue abuts the anterior margin  The posterior margin is greater than 1cm away from the posterior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE left mastectomy specimen  with a stitch placed by the surgeon  denoting the axillary region  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin black  The specimen is thinly sectioned  to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma with no masses  Dissection of the axillary region reveals no lymph nodes  Representative sections of the more fibrous regions of the normal appearing breast are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left axillary node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm soft tissue specimen with a single lymph node  The surgeon confirms that this is a sentinel node and is from the left side  The specimen is bisected and submitted in toto in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right mastectomy flap   is a 21 0cm in length  1 3cm in diameter and 0 4cm strip of unremarkable skin  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left mastectomy flap   is a 24 0cm in length  0 9cm in diameter and 0 6cm in depth  strip of unremarkable skin  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL   1   EXCISION PART D  SKIN  RIGHT FLAP   EXCISION PART E  SKIN  LEFT FLAP   EXCISION , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 34 CLINICAL DATA  77 year old with cancer of right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA WITH FEATURES OF DUCTAL AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III  REMOVED_DATE CM  WITH ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMAS  MULTIPLE  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  CYST FORMATION  MICROCALCIFICATIONS WITHIN LOBULES   APOCRINE METAPLASIA AND FIBROSIS  NOTE  No definite lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY DISSECTION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 45                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm skin ellipse containing a 4 5cm well healed scar and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm unremarkable nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm axillary tail is also present with this specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a small REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm cavity  Area surrrounding the biopsy cavity is focally white and focally pink and firm  The biopsy cavity extends to 2 5cm from the closest deep margin  The rest of the breast parenchyma is focally yellow and focally white and grossly unremarkable  Section code  A  representative section of biopsy cavity in relation to deep resection margin B C  biopsy cavity in its entirety D G  additional representative sections of areas surrounding biopsy cavity H I  representative section of breast parenchyma away from biopsy cavity J  representative section of nipple Sectioning of axillary tail reveals eleven soft  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm lymph nodes  Representative sections submitted in cassettes K M  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
