Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  28 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 28 CLINICAL DATA  History of a right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures at least 1 5cm in greatest dimension microscopically  No definite vascular invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 26 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 02 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 9cm  white and yellow fibrofatty portion of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a mixture of adipose tissue  and white  semi rubbery fibrous tissue  There is no grossly suspicious lesion for infiltrating carcinoma that is large enough to freeze  No frozen section is done  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through H  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST RIGHT EXCISION  ILL  DEFINED FIRM AREA  SOMEWHAT SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE TUMOR  BUT TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  SPECIMEN TO BE PROCESSED ONLY FOR PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
