he mass from the posteromedial region of the specimen  I  representative sections of tissue away from the mass  in the superolateral portion of the specimen  Labeled  final shaved margin  are 5 small fragments of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring 7 0x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm in aggregate  Focal areas of this tissue are tan white and firm  The tissue is sectioned to reveal some areas of unremarkable appearing breast parenchyma along with some areas of firm tan white tissue forming a mass  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes J S  Gross Description by  JIM BRADLEY Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE   SENTINEL    REMOVED_CASE_ID   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE   SENTINEL   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D  BREAST  RIGHT  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Radiology Outpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  STEPHANIE L  SHAPIRO  M D  PHOEBE E FREER  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 30 year old woman with epidermal nevus syndrome and right bloody nipple discharge  An MRI at a referring hospital demonstrated an enhancing mass in the right breast  An ultrasound exam demonstrated 2 hypoechoic masses  Mass A is at 9 00 o clock  Mass B is at 3 00 o clock  both are 3cm from nipple  The differential diagnosis for mass A is hamartoma versus fibroadenoma  The differential diagnosis for mass B is a cyst versus fibroadenoma versus hamartoma  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  RIGHT  9 00   CORE BIOPSY 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 2  COMPLEX SCLEROSING INTRADUCTAL PAPILLOMA  SEE NOTE  B  BREAST  RIGHT  3 00   CORE BIOPSY FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH CYST WALL  NOTE  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slides  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern highlights the absence of a myoepithelial layer in areas of invasive ductal carcinoma and supports the diagnosis  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received in formalin  labeled  