Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 19 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessels and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 01 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fibrofatty breast tissue with a suture indicating a firm area  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a firm fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through J  J  contains sutured area   Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  NO AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
