tu  GRADE  1  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the microinvasive focus  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1 and 2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to   0 1cm from the lateral margin and  0 2cm from the superior margin  and is 0 3cm from the posterior margin   STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are both  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3 cm fragment of yellow to red adipose tissue  On palpation  the specimen contains multiple nodules measuring  0 3cm  The specimen is frozen entirely as FX 1 and now resubmitted as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  left breast lump   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0 cm fragment of yellow  lobular breast parenchyma which is oriented with a long stitch indicating lateral and a short stitch indicating superior  The specimen contains three needle localization wires corresponding to areas of interest as noted on the accompanying specimen radiograph  The first wire indicates a posterior medial region of calcifications  A second wire orients a region of a clip in the middle of the specimen  The third wire indicates the region of anterior lateral calcification  The specimen is inked as follows  superior green  inferior yellow  posterior black  anterior blue  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral long axis to reveal three areas of interest corr