est s accuracy and precision  Added by  Rosemary Tambouret MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm irregular tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue with a long suture designating the lateral aspect and a short suture designating the superior aspect  The anterior aspect is inked black  the posterior blue  the superior green and the inferior yellow  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm oval  ill defined  indurated tan pink mass located within the mid portion of the specimen 0 3cm from the posterior  0 5cm from the anterior margin   1 0cm from the superior and inferior margins  0 9cm from the medial  and 1 7cm from the lateral margins  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan yellow  lobulated and unremarkable  The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes A F with the entire nodule in cassettes D E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast medial specimen   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular tan yellow to pink lobulated unoriented portion of fibrofatty tissue  which is inked  sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes G I  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  CHRISTOPHER M  WILLIAM  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST RIGHT MEDIAL  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY 2 , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 53 CLINICAL DATA  63 year old female with biopsy proven right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  90   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10   SINGLE FOCUS  COMEDO TYPE  3  BREAST ATROPHY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Inked resection margins are free of carcinoma  the closest margin is at least 0 5cm  from tumor  There is no evidence of lymphatic or vascular invasion  Carcinoma is present in two of fifteen slides  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fibroadipose tissue with wire in place and x ray demonstrating an ill defined stellate lesion  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm firm gritty region with a central hemorrhagic cavity  This area is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in cassette A  Remaining tissue from that region is submitted in cassette B  Additional representative sections of tissue are submitted in cassettes C through O  Labeled  Axillary contents  is a piece of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm  Several lymph nodes are identified within this tissue  The largest lymph node is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm  The largest two are bisected and submitted entirely in cassettes P and Q  respectively  Remaining lymph nodes in R through T  Resident  Mark vanGorder  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
