been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lumpectomy short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 3cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with localization wire in place and a corresponding radiograph  Two black stitches designates the superior and lateral margins  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the lateral yellow  and the medial green  The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm well defined indurated gray white lesion which comes to 0 2cm of the anterior  0 5cm of the posterior  0 6cm of the medial  0 9cm of the lateral  and greater than 2 0cm of the superior and inferior margin  The remaining cut surface consists of 80  focally indurated dense gray white fibrous tissue and 20  tan yellow adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted from superior to inferior as A F with the lesion as A D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue which is sectioned to reveal 4 gray pink lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm in greatest dimension  The nodes are submitted entirely as follows  G  2 lymph nodes  the larger of which is bisected and inked black  H  2 lymph nodes  one of which is inked black and bisected  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   2 final shaved margins superior right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm aggregate of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue fragment with no orientation  The fragments consist of 95  tan yellow adipose and 5  dense gray white fibrous tissue  and are entirely submitted as I J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins inferior right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of irregular tan yellow fibroadipose tissue fragment with no orientation  Sectioning reveals 85  tan yellow adipose and 15  dense gray white fibrous tissue with no lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as K M  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE SENTINEL   REMOVED_CASE_ID   737  EXCISION PART C  BREAST RIGHT SUPERIOR  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART D  BREAST RIGHT INFERIOR  FINAL SHAVED MARGIN , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 17 02 CLINICAL DATA  78 year old female with known left breast cancer  extensive DCIS                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH APOCRINE FEATURES  EXTENSIVE  FOCALLY INVOLVING A RADIAL SCAR AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  WITH A SMALL   0 4CM  AREA SUSPICIOUS BUT NOT DIAGNOSTIC FOR INVASION  SEE NOTE AND TABLE 1   TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS 1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Involving 7 of 14 blocks  spanning at least 4 0cm  Grade  2 Calcifications  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Margins of resection are free of carcinoma  NOTE  Periductal fibrosis  stromal reactive changes secondary to prior biopsy site  and focal involvement of sclerosing adenosis by in situ carcinoma make it difficult to accurately diagnosis microinvasive carcinoma in this case  The margins of resection are free of carcinoma  2 FOLLICULAR LYMPHOMA WITH SCLEROSIS  GRADE 1 OF 3  INVOLVING 4 OF 9 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The lymphoma has an unusual appearance  some follicles are sclerotic and the lymphoid cells in them are spindled  resembling mesenchymal cells  Immunohistochemical studies will be performed and reported upon in an addendum  3 ALL  9  LYMPH NODES ARE FREE OF BREAST CARCINOMA CELLS  4 RADIAL SCARS  5 FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH PROMINENT SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  6 BIOPSY CHANGES  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 45                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  PARAFFIN SECTIONS OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  With antibody to B lineage antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of most cells in a follicular pattern  The B cells are positive for  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and bcl 2  Follicles are delineated by  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  staining  With antibody to T lineage associated antigen  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  there is staining of many small cells in the interfollcular region  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of follicular lymphoma  The slides from the prior lymph node biopsy have been reviewed   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The findings are similar to those in the current case  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 33     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     With antibody to bcl 6 on a section from the axillary nodes  many of the atypical lymphoid cells are stained  This provides additional support for the diagnosis of follicular lymphoma  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE grams  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  and an anterior tan white skin ellipse  REMOVED_DATE x 8 5cm  with an unremarkable nipple and a 2 5cm well healed linear scar in the lateral portion of the skin  The specimen is inked in black posteriorly and blue anteriorly  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm tan white stellate  vaguely nodular firm mass  with focal areas of calcification and fat necrosis  The tumor mass is present directly subjacent to the skin scar  and comes within 0 7cm of the posterior margin  1 5cm of skin surface  and 2 5cm of anterior margin  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan white firm area is identified in the inner lower quadrant  3 5cm from the main tumor mass  The remainder of the specimen is grossly unremarkable without additional focal lesions  Biopsy cavity is not grossly identified  SECTION CODE  A  The closest posterior margin  B  Anterior margin  C H  Representative of the main tumor mass  I  Satellite tumor  submitted entirely  J K  Grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma from the inner lower quadrant  away from the tumor mass  L  Grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma from the inner upper quadrant  away from the tumor mass  M  Grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma from the outer lower quadrant  away from the tumor mass  N  Grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma from the outer upper quadrant  away from the tumor mass  O R  Axillary lymph nodes  with the nodes in P and Q  bisected  Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
