Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic and blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast excisional biopsy specimen  with an attached 5 x 0 8cm skin ellipse  The entire specimen is inked black  with the deep margin  posterior  overinked blue  and the superior margin overinked red  It is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a tan gray  1 2cm in largest dimension  firm mass  focally abutting the anterior soft tissue margin  and 0 5cm from the posterior margin  Sectioning of the tissue away from the mass reveals a 0 6cm in largest dimension area of tan grittiness  coming to within 0 3cm of the deep margin  in the medial portion of the specimen  There is a third area of grittiness  0 2cm in largest dimension  coming to within 0 6cm of the deep margin  The remainder of the tissue is mixed white fibrous parenchyma and fatty tissue  SECTION CODE A C  Firm nodule with anterior and posterior margins  D  Representative section of nodule  E  Gritty area  F  Second gritty area  G H  Representative sections  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA CLOSE TO ANTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
