ail  The specimen is inked  anterior blue  posterior deep black  serially sectioned to display an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm area of moderately indurated  dense  white  fibrous tissue located centrally subjacent to the skin and continuous with the posterior deep margin this area is within 1 5cm from the skin surface  Located centrally within the dense white fibrous tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm gray white glistening stellate lesion which comes within 0 4cm from the deep margin  There is blue dye infiltrated at the lateral aspect of the breast  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly tan yellow fat with a minimal amount of dense white fibrous tissue  There are no other lesions noted  Four lymph nodes are identified within the axillary tail  Representative sections are submitted  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   Section code  C D  glistening gray white lesion to deep margin E F  indurated fibrous tissue adjacent to glistening lesion G  glistening gray white lesion at tissue subjacent to nipple  H O  fibrous tissues submitted sequentially from medial to lateral P  three whole axillary lymph nodes  Q  two whole axillary lymph nodes  BB GG  Fibrous breast tissue  HH KK  Remainder of biopsy site and adjacent breast tissue  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional right breast superficial tissue  is a 3 8x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of predominantly tan yellow adipose tissue with approximately 20  dense white fibrous tissue  There are no gross lesions identified  The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in R V  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional upper outer right axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink lymph node  The specimen is submitted in toto as W  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0