OPIC FOCI  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The lobular carcinoma cells do not stain for E cadherin  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left simple mastectomy specimen  There is a stitch designating 12 o clock  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan white  wrinkled portion of attached skin with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm everted nipple  The skin shows a 5 0cm in length well healed scar  which is 4 4cm from the nipple  There is a 0 5cm defect within the posterior margin through which the biopsy cavity communicates  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned from 3 o clock to 9 o clock aspect  The cut surface reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm pink to red  hemorrhagic  fibrotic biopsy cavity  which is grossly communicating with the posterior wall  is 1 8cm from the anterior margin and is located 3 5cm from the stitch which is denoting the 12 o clock aspect  The remaining breast parenchyma is composed of unremarkable adipose tissue with a moderate amount of tan white unremarkable fibrous tissue  A few small tan cysts filled with clear  watery fluid are identified throughout the breast parenchyma  No other masses or lesions are identified  The sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from biopsy cavities to include anterior and posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from 3 o clock aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section from 6 o clock aspect   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of cyst  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast   is 