Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 00 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 00 at 12 51 CLINICAL DATA  Known left breast carcinoma DCIS  high grade with microinvasion  Reviewed at Brigham   Women s Hospital                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL 1 2   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWO OF TWO SENTINEL LYMPH NODES   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Immunohistochemical stains for keratin on multiple levels reveal no positively staining tumor cells  B  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   AND FOCAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU GRADE 3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasive carcinoma is not identified  The ductal carcinoma in situ  resembling the tumor removed previously  is present in two blocks  Foci interpreted as representing lobular neoplasia  some with features intermediate between lobular and ductal neoplasia  are scattered throughout many sections  most prominently in fibrous areas  The posterior margin in examined sections appears free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 00 at 17 22                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan blue lymph node  bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  and now submitted as cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and   2 left axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white lymph node  The fat has been trimmed and the node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 2  now submitted as cassette B  Received fresh   label