ng the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  breast left modified radical mastectomy   is a 423 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 8cm specimen that consists of an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE breast and REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm of axillary tissue  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior  black  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan white areola consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm nipple that appears grossly unremarkable  There is a semi circular scar over the superomedial aspect of the areola  Within the breast tissue underlying the superomedial scar is a poorly delineated  tan white fibrous area consistent with a scar  measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm  About 0 5cm superior and adjoining this fibrous region  is an irregular  tan whitish yellow firm stellate lesion  that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  and is located 0 4cm from the anterior margin and 2 0cm from the closest posterior margin  This lesion is located in the mid superior quadrant  In the outer quadrant  around the 3 o clock position  is a poorly delineated  REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm biopsy cavity associated with hemorrhage and calcification  The biopsy cavity appears mildly hard to firm in consistency  The area of firmness is located 1 2cm from the closest posterior margin  and 0 7cm from the closest anterior margin  Also noted are multiple tan white fibrocystic areas that are predominantly located in the center and lower inner quadrant of the breast  The axillary tissue is dissected for lymph nodes  multiple potential lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Section Code   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Stellate lesion  superior breast  to the posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Stellate lesion to the anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION