gnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right axillary sentinel node biopsy  276   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm possible lymph node which is bivalved and frozen entirely as FX 1 and FX 1A  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right axillary sentinel node  326   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm possible lymph node with a scant amount of attached tan yellow fat  The specimen is frozen entirely as FX 2  now as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Quinn  REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm oriented right simple mastectomy specimen  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm nipple  which is grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm stellate scar in the upper inner quadrant approximately between 1 and 2 o clock position  which lies 0 6cm from overlying inked margin and 1 5cm from superior inked margin  The breast parenchyma surrounding the scar contains foci of fat necrosis and is focally nodular and gritty in feel  The remaining breast parenchyma contains approximately 50  tan white rubbery fibrous tissue predominant in the inner and central quadrants with numerous blue domed cysts  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  In the central quadrant approximately 5 0cm lateral to the biopsy site  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan white  fairly well circumscribed nodule  lies 2 5cm from overlying anterior and 2 5cm from posterior inked margin  The nodule is bisected to reveal a tan 