ntained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm left radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm skin ellipse containing a 1 0cm unremarkable nipple  2 0cm from the nipple is a 1 5cm well healed linear surgical scar  The axillary tail is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm biopsy cavity  0 3cm from the nearest inked deep margin  The biopsy cavity is beneath the previously described surgical scar  in the medial inferior aspect of the specimen  The remaining breast parenchyma contains multiple cysts  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 0cm in greatest dimension  The cysts are filled with clear yellow to green fluid  The remaining breast parenchyma is firm  white  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple rubbery  tan to pink lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 8cm in greatest dimension  SECTION CODE  A I  axillary lymph nodes J M  representative sections of biopsy cavity and adjacent deep inked margin from medial to lateral N  sections just lateral to biopsy cavity O  representative section of cyst  at least 3 0cm away from biopsy cavity P  representative sections of nipple  Resident  Cynthia E  Flynn  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
