ms of axillary involvement  None  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 1cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm attached axillary tail  Along the anterior aspect  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 16 8cm portion of tan brown and edematous skin displaying mild dimpling around the slightly retracted nipple  There is a suture designating 12 o clock  The anterior aspect is inked blue  and the posterior black  On sectioning  the parenchyma consists of tan white  dense fibrous tissue and yellow  lobulated fat  No discrete lesions are identified  Ten potential lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tail ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 1cm in greatest dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One quadrisected node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Four intact nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One bisected tissue fragment in each  Gross Dictation by Rebecca J DiIorio  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Rebecca J DiIorio  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Some tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA 