Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  28 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  28 MAY 98 at 12 36 CLINICAL DATA  58 year old female patient with a 1cm hypo echoic mass at the 9 o clock position                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  9 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 17 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number are 10 cores of soft  tan tissue  ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm which are submitted in toto as A  Gross Description by  Robert F Donnell Resident  RICHARD AMMER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Zareh Nazareth Demirjian  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  Jaime L Kline  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY , Unchecked.
